perl-cross 1.6.5: --hints=<name> loads nothing

cnf/configure_hint.sh calls `tryhints 'hint' "$h"` for each --hints entry,
so it looks for cnf/hints/hint and never loads the named file. For
wasix-perl every target size probe then runs readelf on wasm objects
("Cannot determine sizeof(char)"). Applied by build.sh to the perl-cross
overlay (patch -p1 in the perl source). homescoop#182.

--- a/cnf/configure_hint.sh
+++ b/cnf/configure_hint.sh
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@
 
 if [ -n "$userhints" ]; then
 	for h in `echo "$userhints" | sed -e 's/,/ /g'`; do
-		tryhints 'hint' "$h"
+		tryhints "$h"
 	done
 else
 	tryhints "$archname"
